From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sepolicy: lsblk may read the udev database

On NickelOS Unified, lsblk is Gentoo's util-linux 2.42, which reads a
device's properties from udev's database (/run/udev/data) as distributions
expect; cros_lsblk could not, and every call was denied (os_install_service
lists disks with it). cros_chromeos_install, cryptohomed and spaced already
read it.

---
diff -ruN a/sepolicy/policy/chromeos/cros_lsblk.te b/sepolicy/policy/chromeos/cros_lsblk.te
--- a/sepolicy/policy/chromeos/cros_lsblk.te
+++ b/sepolicy/policy/chromeos/cros_lsblk.te
@@ -23,4 +23,9 @@
 allow cros_lsblk sysfs_zram:dir { open read search };
 allow cros_lsblk sysfs_zram:file { getattr open read };
 
+# NickelOS: util-linux's lsblk reads a device's properties from udev's
+# database.
+allow cros_lsblk cros_run_udev:dir r_dir_perms;
+allow cros_lsblk cros_run_udev:file r_file_perms;
+
 allowxperm cros_lsblk cros_os_install_service:fifo_file ioctl TIOCGWINSZ;
